From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:48:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] hc read: staged down projection on 81 / 162 blocks,
 bitwise the same (opt-in STRATA_GR_DOWN_SPLIT=2|4)

The staged down projection runs 8 rows a block, 41 blocks: half of an RTX 3090's 82 SMs idle, and each busy SM
reads 8 rows of weights and runs 8 rows x T tokens of shared-memory dots (2 LDS.128 per 8 FMA, the per-SM
shared-memory bandwidth grows with T). STRATA_GR_DOWN_SPLIT=2 / 4 gives a block 4 / 2 rows (81 / 162 blocks).
Each row is still one warp with the same chunks per lane in the same order and the same xor tree, so every
output is the same bits. Only for the exact-token launches (multi-GR on); 4 is taken as 2 above 4 tokens.
Default path: all 89 fused_gr kernels SASS-identical to g3-1441-ll (cuobjdump, the staged kernels' names gained
a trailing ROWS = 8). gr_parity ctest arms: down_split2, down_split4_pf2 (with the production switches),
down_split2_pf3; fused_gr_bench's cold run ends with SPLIT lines (41 / 81 / 162 blocks in one process, bitwise
against 41, with times).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
